coverage/
.vitest/

# Editor / OS cruft
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Local governance / architecture docs — not part of the shipped module.
governance/

# End-to-end harness. The *source* is tracked: it drives a real Foundry install against real
# content modules and is where a good deal of this module's advancement behaviour is verified.
# It is never shipped — the release archive in `.github/workflows/main.yml` names its contents
# explicitly rather than packaging the repo — so being tracked and being released are separate
# questions. Three things stay out:
#
#   config.mjs  absolute paths to one machine's Foundry install and user data
#   run output  the diffs and the generated report quote item descriptions verbatim, which for
#               the content modules under test means text from paid packs; this repo is public
#   bulk        each results file is ~2 MB
#
# `config.example.mjs` is tracked in its place; copy it to `config.mjs` and edit the paths.
test-e2e/config.mjs
test-e2e/*.log
test-e2e/*.jsonl
test-e2e/*.html
# Dropped by shell.mjs and screenshots.mjs when a run fails — a picture of the broken world.
test-e2e/failure.png
